---
description: Proper handling of Personally Identifiable Information (PII) in compliance with GDPR
alwaysApply: true
---

pii-handling:

- Identify and classify all PII data (names, emails, phone numbers, addresses, IPs, etc.)
- Implement data minimization - only collect necessary PII
- Encrypt PII at rest and in transit
- Implement proper access controls for PII
- Log all PII access for audit trails
- Provide mechanisms for data export (right to data portability)
- Implement data deletion capabilities (right to be forgotten)
- Anonymize or pseudonymize PII where possible

PII categories to protect:
- Direct identifiers: Name, email, phone, SSN, passport number
- Indirect identifiers: IP address, device ID, cookies, location data
- Sensitive data: Health records, financial data, biometric data, racial/ethnic origin

Good practices:
```javascript
// Encrypt PII before storage
const encryptedEmail = encrypt(userEmail);
await db.users.create({ email: encryptedEmail });

// Anonymize for analytics
const anonymizedData = {
  userId: hash(user.id),
  action: user.action,
  // Remove PII fields
};
```

Bad practices to avoid:
```javascript
// Storing PII in plain text
await db.users.create({ email: userEmail, ssn: userSSN });

// Logging PII
console.log('User email:', user.email);
```
